: "Opening Hook", "concise_summary": "The candidate has submitted a blank booklet page with no substantive arguments or text.", "verbatim_quote": "...", "what_stage_contributes": "Does not contribute any argument towards the central essay topic.", "transition_or_gap": "Complete absence of response.", "status": "drift", "status_label": "Concluding Synthesis"}], "intro_audit": {"intro_score": 5.0, "intro_max": 20.0, "intro_archetype": "Anecdotal Hook", "topic_vs_question_relevance": "Zero content provided to evaluate relevance.", "current_critique": "The candidate''s booklet is entirely blank. For the UPSC Mains Essay paper, failing to write an essay results in a zero for the paper, severely impacting overall rank and selection prospects.", "opening_passage": "..."}, "body_audit": {"body_score": 17.5, "body_max": 90.0, "strengths": ["None identified due to blank submission."], "critical_gaps": ["Entire essay body is missing (Page 1).", "Failure to engage with any dimensions of the essay topic ''Courage is resistance to fear, mastery of fear, not absence of fear''."], "missing_dimensions": ["Philosophical and ethical dimensions of fear and courage.", "Historical and political resistance movements.", "Socio-economic vulnerabilities and administrative courage.", "Psychological mastery of fear in modern life."], "examiner_guidance": "Ensure time management in the examination hall so that all assigned essay topics are attempted. Even a structured outline with basic arguments yields better marks than a blank page."}, "conclusion_audit": {"conclusion_score": 2.5, "conclusion_max": 15.0, "conclusion_archetype": "Cohesive Synthesis", "failure_mode": "Abrupt Ending", "current_critique": "No conclusion was written.", "way_ahead_prescriptions": "Practice full-length essay writing under timed conditions to build stamina and prevent leaving booklets blank."}, "point_by_point_audit": [{"page": 1, "title": "Stage 1: Blank Page", "what_you_wrote": "...", "evaluator_remark": "No text written on this page. Please ensure regular writing practice.", "examiner_verdict": "Unattempted", "verdict": "Superficial", "badge": "Philosophical Hook"}], "visual_annotations": [{"page": 1, "box_2d": [100, 100, 300, 900], "quote": "...", "label": "Examiner Margin Note", "tag": "Examiner Margin Note", "remark": "Unattempted essay booklet page. Zero marks awarded.", "text": "Unattempted essay booklet page. Zero marks awarded.", "type": "critical", "start_y_percent": 10.0, "end_y_percent": 30.0}], "revision_priorities": [{"title": "Complete Examination Attempt", "page": 1, "candidate_exact_passage": "...", "evaluator_diagnosis": "The candidate did not write any content for the 125-mark essay question.", "actionable_guidance": "Develop a structured template for essay writing including introduction, multi-dimensional body paragraphs, and a visionary conclusion.", "optional_example_rewrite": "Mark Twain once noted, ''Courage is resistance to fear, mastery of fear, not absence of fear''\u2014a profound reminder that bravery is not the absence of terror, but the triumph over it."}], "rubric_scores": {"intro_score": 0.0, "core_demand_score": 0.0, "value_add_score": 0.0, "presentation_score": 0.0, "context_score": 0.0}, "upsc_exam_hall_discipline": {"estimated_word_count": 2, "estimated_writing_time_mins": "Unavailable", "word_budget_status": "Under target (2 words)", "margin_discipline": "Maintained strictly", "handwriting_legibility": "Clean & Readable"}, "next_attempt_focus": {"thesis_crystallization": "Ensure every essay begins with a clear philosophical framing of the core quote.", "student_draft_quote": "...", "booklet_placement": "Page 1, Paragraph 1", "examiner_upgrade_sentence": "True courage is forged not in the absence of peril, but in the deliberate mastery of one''s deepest anxieties."}, "model_answer": "Introduction: Open with Mark Twain''s definition or a reflection on human vulnerability. Define courage not as fearlessness (like a reckless machine), but as moral and physical endurance in the face of terror. Body Paragraphs: 1. Philosophical Dimension: Aristotle''s Golden Mean between cowardice and rashness. 2. Historical Dimension: Nelson Mandela or Mahatma Gandhi acknowledging fear while fighting systemic oppression. 3. Socio-Economic Dimension: Marginalized sections overcoming systemic barriers despite fear of failure or reprisal. 4. Administrative Dimension: Civil servants standing up to political corruption or handling disaster management amidst uncertainty. Conclusion: Synthesize that fear is a natural evolutionary guardrail, but courage is the human agency that transforms fear into purposeful action.", "transcribed_text": "[Page 1]\n", "pages": ["data:image/jpeg;base64,"], "page_ledger": {"1": {"original_page_number": 1, "status": "processed", "role": "Blank page", "word_count": 0, "uncertain_spans_count": 0}}, "_meta_eval_id": "eval_1792243539_0fd39e", "_meta_created_at": "2026-10-17 13:25:39", "created_at": "2026-10-17 13:25:39", "evaluated_at": "2026-10-17 13:25:39", "_meta_user_email": "guest@cookedmains.in", "_meta_paper": "Essay", "_meta_max_marks": 125, "_meta_is_rewrite": 0, "_meta_baseline_eval_id": null, "_meta_file_hash": null, "_meta_visual_hashes": ["0000000000000000"], "_meta_thumbnail": "data:image/jpeg;base64,", "_meta_pages": ["data:image/jpeg;base64,"]}', '["data:image/jpeg;base64,"]', 'data:image/jpeg;base64,', 0, '', 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-10-17 13:25:39')
